        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arc93" edge="1" parent="1" source="arc88" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#555555;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;edgeStyle=elbowEdgeStyle;elbow=vertical;endArrow=none;strokeColor=#999999;strokeWidth=2;" target="arc71" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arc94" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;arcSize=8;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;" value="&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:15px&#39;&gt;Key design decisions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&#39;font-size:12px&#39;&gt;1. Every API has the same skeleton. A new API is a copy of an existing API folder.&lt;br&gt;2. Testers write only in &lt;b&gt;projects/&lt;/b&gt;; the framework writes only in &lt;b&gt;baselines/&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br&gt;3. Endpoint definitions are TypeScript: mistakes fail at compile time, not during a run.&lt;br&gt;4. Project and API names come from folder names, so they can never mismatch.&lt;br&gt;5. The framework has its own unit tests; every pull request runs typecheck, lint and tests.&lt;br&gt;6. Adding a project, API, endpoint or test case never requires a change in src/.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="616" x="40" y="980" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arc95" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;arcSize=8;align=left;spacingLeft=12;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;" value="&lt;b style=&#39;font-size:15px&#39;&gt;How to run&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&#39;font-size:12px&#39;&gt;Everything: npx playwright test&lt;br&gt;One project: npx playwright test projects/prj-a&lt;br&gt;One API: npx playwright test projects/prj-a/api-crew&lt;br&gt;One mode: add --project=comparison or --project=regression&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="616" x="988" y="840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arc96" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;arcSize=8;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Blue:&lt;/b&gt; written by testers" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="34" width="300" x="40" y="1300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
